def is_convex_polygon(points):
    if len(points) < 3:
        return False
    n = len(points)
    cross = lambda i: (points[i][1] - points[i - 1][1]) * (points[(i + 1) % n][0] - points[i][0]) - (
        points[i][0] - points[i - 1][0]) * (points[(i + 1) % n][1] - points[i][1])
    sign = None
    for i in range(n):
        c = cross(i)
        if c == 0:
            return False
        if sign is None:
            sign = 1 if c > 0 else -1
        elif (c > 0 and sign < 0) or (c < 0 and sign > 0):
            return False
    return True
```

This implementation checks the direction of the turn between each triple of consecutive points by computing the signed area of the parallelogram formed by the two edges meeting at the middle point. If the sign of this cross product changes across any vertex, the polygon has an interior angle greater than 180 degrees and is not convex. A zero cross product indicates collinearity, which also disqualifies the polygon as convex. The function loops through all vertices once, so it runs in linear time.

